## Configuration

Call `load_settings()` once at startup, then pass settings to the modules that need
them. It reads environment variables and defaults; files require explicit
selection with {% if config_file %}`config_file=Path("config.toml")`, {% endif %}`env_file=Path(".env")` or `secrets_dir=Path("/run/secrets")`.

```bash
uv run {{ project_slug }} {% if config_file %}--config config.toml {% endif %}--env-file .env info
```

Priority is constructor overrides, environment variables, the selected dotenv file,
the selected secret files, {% if config_file %}the selected config file, {% endif %}then defaults. All relative paths use the
working directory. {% if config_file %}`.env.example` and `config.example.toml` list{% else %}`.env.example` lists{% endif %} every supported key;
secret filenames use the same nested names. Explicit missing paths fail at startup.
